1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,870
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,380
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:05,840
(Episode 17)

4
00:00:07,410 --> 00:00:09,410
Let's see.

5
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:11,380
(Delinquent Account Management
and Collection Review Report)

6
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:14,950
A 45-year-old man.
He has a good job.

7
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:17,560
Why is his salary so high?

8
00:00:19,290 --> 00:00:21,890
I guess this is how he could
take out such a large loan.

9
00:00:23,130 --> 00:00:26,560
But where did he put all that money
if he doesn't have it now?

10
00:00:27,870 --> 00:00:28,870
Next.

11
00:00:29,770 --> 00:00:31,670
(Delinquent Account Management
and Collection Review Report)

12
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:35,810
Grandma reads faces,
and his eyes look too fierce.

13
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:37,440
His pupils are cloudy, too.

14
00:00:38,610 --> 00:00:39,610
Pass.

15
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:41,250
(Delinquent Account Management
and Collection Review Report)

16
00:00:41,310 --> 00:00:42,910
(Debtor Summary, Name: Kang Dae Chi)

17
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:44,350
His name is Dae Chi?

18
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:46,520
What? Was he born in Daechi-dong?

19
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,390
He's somewhat handsome.

20
00:00:49,820 --> 00:00:50,920
Purchasing department
at a big company?

21
00:00:51,720 --> 00:00:53,120
He looks like
a regular office worker,

22
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:55,730
so how did he end up
with so much debt?

23
00:00:56,260 --> 00:00:58,100
He gives a good impression.

24
00:00:58,760 --> 00:00:59,760
All right.

25
00:01:00,230 --> 00:01:01,430
You're the one,
my ticket to business.

26
00:01:02,870 --> 00:01:06,070
Get out, all of you.
I said, get out.

27
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:14,210
You're up early today, sweetie.

28
00:01:14,610 --> 00:01:17,720
Dad, do you think I just
laze around every day?

29
00:01:18,720 --> 00:01:20,150
By the way,

30
00:01:20,150 --> 00:01:22,450
why did Grandma yell at you
and Mom to get out?

31
00:01:24,220 --> 00:01:25,220
Did you do something wrong, Mom?

32
00:01:25,690 --> 00:01:26,760
It's not like that.

33
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:29,430
But Se Na, what were you doing?

34
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:30,760
Grandma's mission.

35
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:34,300
I finally...

36
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:36,940
found an investor
for the Cha Se Na brand.

37
00:01:37,470 --> 00:01:38,800
If I collect this person's debt...

38
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:40,810
What?

39
00:01:40,870 --> 00:01:42,570
She told you to collect
this entire amount?

40
00:01:42,970 --> 00:01:44,780
Grandma did?
When she was in her right mind?

41
00:01:49,010 --> 00:01:52,380
Honey, Se Na is still young
and needs to study.

42
00:01:52,450 --> 00:01:54,950
She shouldn't do debt collection.

43
00:01:54,950 --> 00:01:56,350
Now that Grandma has stepped in,

44
00:01:56,420 --> 00:01:58,320
you know it's no use...

45
00:01:58,660 --> 00:01:59,790
no matter how much
you two object, right?

46
00:02:00,790 --> 00:02:02,290
I'll make the coffee today.

47
00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:09,730
But honey,

48
00:02:09,930 --> 00:02:12,940
what exactly was inside
that black plastic bag earlier...

49
00:02:13,470 --> 00:02:15,870
for Mother to hide it like that?

50
00:02:17,180 --> 00:02:19,040
I have a guess.

51
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:20,380
What is it?

52
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:23,080
Dollars.

53
00:02:23,850 --> 00:02:24,980
Dollars?

54
00:02:25,550 --> 00:02:29,590
Back when my mother was young,
she used to deal in dollars.

55
00:02:30,190 --> 00:02:32,360
Since then,
she would always stash...

56
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:35,230
dollars in a black plastic bag
as an emergency fund.

57
00:02:35,490 --> 00:02:36,760
That's probably what it is.

58
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:40,600
But why go to such lengths
for dollars?

59
00:02:44,970 --> 00:02:48,110
Come to think of it,
I have not really run much...

60
00:02:48,170 --> 00:02:50,110
while wearing a skirt
and sneakers...

61
00:02:50,510 --> 00:02:53,240
For one, do people not usually
wear heels with skirts?

62
00:02:54,710 --> 00:02:55,710
Anyway, I...

63
00:02:55,850 --> 00:02:59,120
always try to wear clothes and shoes
that fit the time and place.

64
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:01,190
Like a proper Hwanggeum Apparel employee.

65
00:03:02,950 --> 00:03:03,960
That is not what I meant.

66
00:03:05,060 --> 00:03:09,190
A while ago, I saw a woman running
in a skirt and sneakers,

67
00:03:09,990 --> 00:03:11,100
and she looked great.

68
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:13,800
It was a unique look that was...

69
00:03:13,870 --> 00:03:16,670
formal yet casual and trendy,
something like that.

70
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:18,770
So I was thinking,

71
00:03:18,870 --> 00:03:20,970
how about we release sneakers
that would go well with skirts...

72
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:24,040
- for this season?
- Where did you see this?

73
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:25,210
At a tennis match or something?

74
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:26,880
No.

75
00:03:27,050 --> 00:03:28,750
It was a woman I saw
at the department store,

76
00:03:29,310 --> 00:03:31,180
and she was so memorable
that I keep thinking about her.

77
00:03:32,020 --> 00:03:33,250
Enough to lose sleep over.

78
00:03:36,020 --> 00:03:38,090
Did she do track and field
or something?

79
00:03:39,590 --> 00:03:40,830
Anyway, Team Leader Cha,

80
00:03:40,990 --> 00:03:42,360
you are focusing
on the sneakers, right?

81
00:03:42,490 --> 00:03:45,260
Yes, let us plan it out anyway.

82
00:03:50,970 --> 00:03:52,240
Oh, right, Team Leader Cha.

83
00:03:53,170 --> 00:03:55,610
What? He was just
right in front of me.

84
00:03:59,140 --> 00:04:01,650
How annoying,
he just said his piece and left?

85
00:04:03,450 --> 00:04:04,450
Still...

86
00:04:04,950 --> 00:04:07,190
I knew I could not
just keep pulling.

87
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:10,290
I pushed a little,
and he talked to me first.

88
00:04:14,690 --> 00:04:15,690
Gang Nam, where is Su Ah?

89
00:04:16,330 --> 00:04:18,360
She slept in Grandma's room.

90
00:04:20,130 --> 00:04:21,330
Then give this to Su Ah.

91
00:04:23,130 --> 00:04:26,900
That's my girl!

92
00:04:27,570 --> 00:04:30,170
Even the stingy Kkangda
opened her wallet.

93
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:32,440
Thank you, little sister.

94
00:04:37,150 --> 00:04:39,450
Is he not going to work?
What is wrong with him?

95
00:04:39,750 --> 00:04:41,320
What? Good question.

96
00:04:42,550 --> 00:04:43,590
Hey, Kang Dae Chi.

97
00:04:44,490 --> 00:04:45,490
Are you not going to work?

98
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:50,400
- Hey, punk.
- Seriously, come on!

99
00:04:50,860 --> 00:04:53,000
I am up!

100
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:54,670
You startled me.

101
00:04:55,870 --> 00:04:57,440
Hey, you have to go to work.

102
00:04:57,700 --> 00:04:58,800
I am going.

103
00:04:59,470 --> 00:05:00,470
That stupid company.

104
00:05:03,910 --> 00:05:06,280
The CEO might have noticed.

105
00:05:07,050 --> 00:05:09,450
I think it would be best
to frequently change...

106
00:05:09,450 --> 00:05:12,280
- where you keep it.
- Yes.

107
00:05:17,860 --> 00:05:19,590
I have been taking sleep aids...

108
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:23,130
for days now.

109
00:05:23,830 --> 00:05:25,500
I thought I would be able
to sleep soundly...

110
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:28,000
once our Seung Yun returned.

111
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:30,370
Somehow...

112
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:33,810
my body and mind are not in sync.

113
00:05:34,110 --> 00:05:36,670
When is Seung Yun
going to start going to the office?

114
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:39,140
He went to work today.

115
00:05:40,780 --> 00:05:41,980
Have you heard anything...

116
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:46,280
- from Seung Yun directly?
- Since he thinks...

117
00:05:46,420 --> 00:05:47,620
I am not in my right mind,

118
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:50,220
it must have been
a huge shock to him.

119
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:53,960
He is just keeping his mouth shut.

120
00:05:54,260 --> 00:05:57,400
As for the documents
you gathered for me last time,

121
00:05:57,830 --> 00:06:00,100
I looked through them all
very carefully.

122
00:06:01,770 --> 00:06:03,030
Did you find any leads?

123
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:06,740
How could I find a lead
that even you missed?

124
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:09,810
But one thing is certain.

125
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:12,840
This is not an accident
we can just overlook.

126
00:06:13,750 --> 00:06:16,610
The grass, the streetlights,

127
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:18,780
even the wind that blew past
there that day...

128
00:06:18,850 --> 00:06:21,550
If I could just catch them,
I would grab them and ask.

129
00:06:22,350 --> 00:06:25,390
What did they see?
To my son, my daughter-in-law,

130
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:27,290
and my young grandson...

131
00:06:27,930 --> 00:06:29,090
What in the world...

132
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:32,760
happened to them there that day?
That is what I want to know.

133
00:06:33,930 --> 00:06:35,970
Even though I have been
by your side for a long time,

134
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:39,340
I have not been of much help,
and I am truly sorry for that.

135
00:06:40,170 --> 00:06:42,140
Nonsense.

136
00:06:44,710 --> 00:06:45,710
Tell me.

137
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:48,980
How are the preparations
for opening your clinic going?

138
00:06:49,280 --> 00:06:53,220
Yes, it will be a small clinic,
so there is not much to prepare.

139
00:06:53,550 --> 00:06:55,450
The fact that my son called you...

140
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:58,460
all the way to the company
to meet with you...

141
00:06:59,620 --> 00:07:03,900
is proof that he has started
to suspect you.

142
00:07:04,460 --> 00:07:07,530
The same goes
for my daughter-in-law, right?

143
00:07:08,300 --> 00:07:09,700
I think so too.

144
00:07:10,100 --> 00:07:12,470
It is better for you
to have outside activities.

145
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:19,880
- Then, Madam Chairwoman...
- I have my suspicions too.

146
00:07:21,010 --> 00:07:23,710
It might not be a solid lead,

147
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:26,750
but maybe a small thread?

148
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:29,390
Or a tiny crack, perhaps?

149
00:07:29,950 --> 00:07:32,160
There is definitely a leak.

150
00:07:32,890 --> 00:07:36,030
Somewhere in this family,

151
00:07:36,090 --> 00:07:40,300
there is definitely someone
who is harboring anxiety.

152
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:48,540
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

153
00:07:52,310 --> 00:07:55,280
This is the right place.

154
00:07:58,020 --> 00:08:00,150
What is this familiar feeling?

155
00:08:01,050 --> 00:08:04,190
I am suddenly getting chills.

156
00:08:05,020 --> 00:08:06,720
Why do I feel so creeped out?

157
00:08:09,590 --> 00:08:11,800
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

158
00:08:16,470 --> 00:08:18,500
Oh my goodness,
how is this possible?

159
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:20,710
How is this possible?

160
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:22,510
What do I do?

161
00:08:23,070 --> 00:08:24,080
What do I do?

162
00:08:26,540 --> 00:08:29,050
I told Ri Ja to boil
the soybean paste in advance,

163
00:08:29,450 --> 00:08:31,050
but she never listens to me.

164
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:35,720
Why are you leaving so late?

165
00:08:36,820 --> 00:08:37,820
Did you eat?

166
00:08:38,460 --> 00:08:39,720
I can go in late today.

167
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:42,560
What about your meal?

168
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:48,400
Mom.

169
00:08:49,430 --> 00:08:50,700
Up until now...

170
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:53,070
I have been a son
you could be proud of.

171
00:08:54,170 --> 00:08:55,610
Out of all your children,

172
00:08:55,710 --> 00:08:58,210
I was the best at studying
and made the most money.

173
00:08:58,780 --> 00:08:59,840
So...

174
00:09:00,310 --> 00:09:02,350
can you just let me off the hook
for the next few years?

175
00:09:03,710 --> 00:09:05,150
You are very capable.

176
00:09:06,050 --> 00:09:07,250
Get a grip on yourself...

177
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:08,450
and just focus on working hard at work.

178
00:09:09,290 --> 00:09:10,790
Mom cannot do that for you.

179
00:09:12,590 --> 00:09:14,130
Rise from recruit to executive...

180
00:09:14,190 --> 00:09:15,290
and become president.

181
00:09:16,160 --> 00:09:17,460
Succeed so that everyone can see.

182
00:09:25,070 --> 00:09:27,270
Oh, my goodness.

183
00:09:29,770 --> 00:09:31,080
Where should I go?

184
00:09:32,680 --> 00:09:35,250
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

185
00:09:38,350 --> 00:09:39,850
(Surgery Consent Form,
Internal Data Document)

186
00:09:47,530 --> 00:09:50,460
You have a nursing assistant
certificate.

187
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:53,830
As you can see,
we are preparing to open,

188
00:09:53,900 --> 00:09:55,400
so the inside is a bit messy.

189
00:09:56,100 --> 00:09:58,100
When can you start working?

190
00:09:58,500 --> 00:10:02,440
Excuse me? I can start working
right this moment.

191
00:10:02,870 --> 00:10:03,870
Yes.

192
00:10:04,310 --> 00:10:05,940
The probationary period
is three months,

193
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:07,750
and after three months,

194
00:10:07,910 --> 00:10:09,780
your annual salary
will be 32,000 dollars.

195
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:11,650
Would that be acceptable?

196
00:10:13,780 --> 00:10:14,790
Really?

197
00:10:14,990 --> 00:10:18,320
I have had a long gap in my career,

198
00:10:18,390 --> 00:10:19,490
and you are going to pay me
that much?

199
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:21,390
I am very grateful.

200
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:23,790
If it is not too much to ask,

201
00:10:24,060 --> 00:10:26,400
would you be able
to start working today?

202
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:28,130
There is not much for you to do,

203
00:10:28,270 --> 00:10:29,700
but I would appreciate it
if you could help...

204
00:10:29,770 --> 00:10:30,770
with the opening preparations.

205
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:33,440
Yes, of course, do not worry.

206
00:10:34,470 --> 00:10:38,440
By the way, Doctor,
do you have any plans to move...

207
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:41,510
the clinic to another location?

208
00:10:43,180 --> 00:10:44,980
No, I do not.

209
00:10:47,390 --> 00:10:51,460
Then how long do you plan
to practice here?

210
00:10:51,460 --> 00:10:53,260
I signed a five-year contract.

211
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:55,030
The location is great,

212
00:10:55,330 --> 00:10:57,760
and the landlord is
a very nice person.

213
00:11:00,870 --> 00:11:01,870
I see.

214
00:11:04,070 --> 00:11:05,140
I am in trouble.

215
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:08,010
How am I going to commute
from now on?

216
00:11:22,550 --> 00:11:24,990
Can you manage me well
as the head designer?

217
00:11:25,490 --> 00:11:28,390
No, can you manage me well,
Team Leader Cha?

218
00:11:28,460 --> 00:11:30,430
I might be fine normally,

219
00:11:30,490 --> 00:11:32,800
but when I work, I am quite sensitive.

220
00:11:32,860 --> 00:11:34,630
And a bit intense, too.

221
00:11:36,070 --> 00:11:38,000
I have already gathered
all the information...

222
00:11:38,070 --> 00:11:40,500
about designer Jaden Cha.

223
00:11:41,340 --> 00:11:43,140
I look forward to working with you.

224
00:11:43,540 --> 00:11:45,780
The company will not hold back
on providing the best support.

225
00:11:49,010 --> 00:11:52,820
When we were young,
my little brother would freak out...

226
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:57,120
if a frog just jumped out of a pond.
When did you grow up so much?

227
00:12:01,290 --> 00:12:03,460
I was wondering
when you would return from the US,

228
00:12:04,100 --> 00:12:05,300
but time really flies.

229
00:12:06,460 --> 00:12:07,500
I feel the same way.

230
00:12:09,870 --> 00:12:10,900
Yes.

231
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:14,070
- Uncle.
- Father.

232
00:12:17,240 --> 00:12:18,310
What brings you here?

233
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:20,140
Did you come to see Mother?

234
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:23,610
No.
I came to see your brother today.

235
00:12:24,850 --> 00:12:28,520
Me? You must be busy. What is it?

236
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:31,020
You should have just called.

237
00:12:31,760 --> 00:12:35,630
I would like our Team Leader Cha
to give us some privacy.

238
00:12:38,700 --> 00:12:40,330
Yes, understood, sir.

239
00:12:50,370 --> 00:12:51,740
What is it, really?

240
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:54,680
I came because
I have something to give you.

241
00:12:56,310 --> 00:12:57,380
What is it?

242
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:07,360
Hey, kid.
It is your first day of work.

243
00:13:09,760 --> 00:13:12,330
Right.
Then again, you are a designer.

244
00:13:23,540 --> 00:13:24,740
This tie...

245
00:13:25,810 --> 00:13:27,380
is yours from now on, Seung Yun.

246
00:13:29,150 --> 00:13:32,220
This is the tie that you, Uncle,

247
00:13:32,280 --> 00:13:34,990
have cherished the most
for a very long time, right?

248
00:13:35,820 --> 00:13:37,220
But why are you giving it to me?

249
00:13:38,520 --> 00:13:40,960
This tie, actually...

250
00:13:42,290 --> 00:13:45,200
Your father,
I mean, my older brother,

251
00:13:46,630 --> 00:13:49,300
when I graduated from college,
gave it to me as a gift.

252
00:13:51,370 --> 00:13:52,770
On the morning of my graduation,

253
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:56,210
your father personally
tied it for me with his own hands.

254
00:13:57,640 --> 00:13:59,310
How to tie it,

255
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:02,410
how to make the knot,

256
00:14:03,510 --> 00:14:06,350
explaining everything slowly,
step by step.

257
00:14:12,990 --> 00:14:16,030
Hoping that a day like this
would surely come,

258
00:14:16,130 --> 00:14:18,560
your Aunt and I raised you,

259
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:23,070
and we waited for you,
who left to study abroad early,

260
00:14:23,070 --> 00:14:24,100
to return safely.

261
00:14:28,870 --> 00:14:31,110
- Uncle.
- Your father,

262
00:14:31,780 --> 00:14:32,840
my brother...

263
00:14:35,110 --> 00:14:36,880
the man named Cha Jun Sung...

264
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:41,690
was always, to me,

265
00:14:42,450 --> 00:14:44,320
the person who taught me my firsts.

266
00:14:45,490 --> 00:14:46,890
He was not just a brother.

267
00:14:49,630 --> 00:14:52,600
He more than filled
our father's empty place...

268
00:14:52,760 --> 00:14:56,100
and was my great mountain
and lighthouse.

269
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:00,500
Seung Yun.

270
00:15:01,840 --> 00:15:03,070
Yes, I'm listening.

271
00:15:03,810 --> 00:15:04,940
I...

272
00:15:05,640 --> 00:15:07,010
and your Aunt...

273
00:15:08,950 --> 00:15:12,350
are standing strong behind you
like a great mountain,

274
00:15:13,580 --> 00:15:16,420
and when you wander
the dark night sea,

275
00:15:16,450 --> 00:15:18,520
we are the lighthouse
that gives you light,

276
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:20,920
so I hope you do not forget that.

277
00:15:22,390 --> 00:15:24,230
Of course,
Grandma will be there for you,

278
00:15:25,700 --> 00:15:27,630
but her health is not so good.

279
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:30,000
Thank you, Uncle.

280
00:15:32,470 --> 00:15:33,470
Right.

281
00:15:38,640 --> 00:15:39,840
No.

282
00:15:43,450 --> 00:15:45,280
They said I cannot be
even one minute late.

283
00:15:47,950 --> 00:15:50,850
Driver, wait a minute.
Please, just a minute.

284
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:52,660
Please, just a minute.

285
00:15:55,690 --> 00:15:56,860
What do I do?

286
00:15:57,060 --> 00:15:59,000
The interval between these buses
is really long.

287
00:16:02,370 --> 00:16:03,430
Taxi.

288
00:16:06,700 --> 00:16:09,070
In all my life, Kang Da Mi,
taking a taxi.

289
00:16:09,710 --> 00:16:11,210
My account is practically empty,

290
00:16:11,280 --> 00:16:12,810
but whatever.

291
00:16:12,880 --> 00:16:15,610
- Welcome, miss.
- Hello, sir.

292
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:17,550
Onjeong Station, Exit Three.

293
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:22,390
Please drive safely.
And a little fast, if possible.

294
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:24,920
What time do you need to arrive?

295
00:16:24,990 --> 00:16:26,990
Two o'clock.
I will not be late, right?

296
00:16:27,490 --> 00:16:29,660
Well, let us see.

297
00:16:30,290 --> 00:16:33,030
The estimated time of arrival
is showing as 1:54.

298
00:16:33,730 --> 00:16:35,930
If nothing happens,
we should make it in time.

299
00:16:36,170 --> 00:16:38,870
- All right, let's get going.
- Thank you.

300
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:55,450
That must be your daughter.

301
00:16:56,290 --> 00:16:58,290
Your wife is beautiful, too.

302
00:16:58,560 --> 00:17:00,060
Yes, thank you.

303
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:04,960
I don't know whose daughter you are,
but you're bright and friendly,

304
00:17:05,260 --> 00:17:08,370
and you're very pretty, too.
Young ladies these days...

305
00:17:08,670 --> 00:17:10,300
aren't all like you.

306
00:17:11,540 --> 00:17:14,470
Really?
You're flattering me too much.

307
00:17:15,840 --> 00:17:18,610
But it looks like
you only have one daughter.

308
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:20,080
Excuse me?

309
00:17:21,150 --> 00:17:22,150
No.

310
00:17:22,380 --> 00:17:24,650
Actually, I have 2 daughters
and 2 sons.

311
00:17:25,080 --> 00:17:26,250
Four in total.

312
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:28,050
Is that so?

313
00:17:28,120 --> 00:17:31,020
- You have a big family.
- Yes, well.

314
00:17:31,320 --> 00:17:33,160
If you're going to Onjeong Station,

315
00:17:33,320 --> 00:17:34,590
you must be going
to the flea market.

316
00:17:35,090 --> 00:17:36,090
Yes.

317
00:17:36,530 --> 00:17:40,000
Young people these days
go to the flea market a lot.

318
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:43,970
It's a world where young people
are actually smarter.

319
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:45,840
Even if they're secondhand clothes,

320
00:17:45,900 --> 00:17:48,610
there are a lot of clothes
that look brand new, actually.

321
00:17:49,110 --> 00:17:50,540
If you go with 100 dollars,

322
00:17:50,710 --> 00:17:52,280
you'll come back
with your arms full.

323
00:17:53,110 --> 00:17:57,010
That's right. Anyway, it's cheap.
That's why we go.

324
00:17:58,620 --> 00:18:02,250
Salaries don't go up easily,
and prices are high.

325
00:18:03,050 --> 00:18:04,350
You're right.

326
00:18:28,310 --> 00:18:31,180
How does it feel
to inherit your father's tie?

327
00:18:31,950 --> 00:18:34,050
I'm touched. And...

328
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:37,590
I feel a sense of responsibility.

329
00:18:39,690 --> 00:18:40,860
Responsibility.

330
00:18:41,990 --> 00:18:43,290
Specifically,

331
00:18:44,460 --> 00:18:46,730
can I ask
what kind of responsibility?

332
00:18:48,530 --> 00:18:52,440
The dreams and work
that my father left behind...

333
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:54,140
before he could
properly unfold them.

334
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:57,840
And my responsibility to Grandma.

335
00:19:01,040 --> 00:19:02,110
You really...

336
00:19:03,410 --> 00:19:05,320
grew up well and came back.

337
00:19:05,880 --> 00:19:08,790
I, your aunt,

338
00:19:09,050 --> 00:19:13,890
am so proud of you, Seung Yun,
and I'm so proud and thankful.

339
00:19:15,330 --> 00:19:16,630
But Seung Yun.

340
00:19:18,260 --> 00:19:20,830
- Yes.
- You are you, Seung Yun.

341
00:19:21,270 --> 00:19:23,270
As designer Jaden Cha,

342
00:19:23,770 --> 00:19:27,500
I want you to run solely toward
your own happiness and dreams.

343
00:19:27,970 --> 00:19:32,210
The duties and burdens
that your parents left behind...

344
00:19:33,410 --> 00:19:36,750
will be shared by me and your uncle,
willingly.

345
00:19:38,450 --> 00:19:42,120
You should live your life freely.

346
00:19:43,890 --> 00:19:44,890
Yes.

347
00:19:46,460 --> 00:19:48,390
You mentioned duties and burdens.

348
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:52,660
Do you two consider Grandma
a duty and a burden?

349
00:19:55,230 --> 00:19:58,300
No. That is absolutely not true.

350
00:19:58,840 --> 00:20:01,370
What I mean is, well...

351
00:20:02,670 --> 00:20:03,940
I was just worried that...

352
00:20:04,440 --> 00:20:07,510
you might feel that way,
which is why I said it.

353
00:20:07,580 --> 00:20:08,980
I think you are misunderstanding me.

354
00:20:10,280 --> 00:20:11,350
Is that so?

355
00:20:12,450 --> 00:20:13,950
I hope it is
just a misunderstanding.

356
00:20:15,350 --> 00:20:17,290
I look forward to working
with you, CEO Jeon.

357
00:20:18,620 --> 00:20:21,730
I will also do my best
for Hwanggeum Apparel.

358
00:20:23,830 --> 00:20:24,930
Are you leaving already?

359
00:20:25,600 --> 00:20:27,060
You have a meeting this afternoon,

360
00:20:27,130 --> 00:20:29,470
so I thought we could
have lunch together before that.

361
00:20:30,230 --> 00:20:33,100
No, I have something to do.
I will be late.

362
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:34,470
I will get going now.

363
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:37,640
I will see you at home.
Good luck with your meeting.

364
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:40,610
Oh, right. Thank you.

365
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:56,060
He came back a different person.

366
00:20:57,490 --> 00:20:58,560
What is it?

367
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:00,660
Why do I feel this chill?

368
00:21:03,430 --> 00:21:04,470
He was just a child.

369
00:21:05,570 --> 00:21:07,540
There is no way
he saw anything back then,

370
00:21:07,640 --> 00:21:08,640
and even if he did,

371
00:21:09,940 --> 00:21:11,410
there is absolutely no way
he remembers.

372
00:21:12,740 --> 00:21:15,110
When he was in the ICU,
the doctor clearly said so.

373
00:21:16,080 --> 00:21:17,680
He had amnesia.

374
00:21:20,120 --> 00:21:21,520
He definitely said that.

375
00:21:47,040 --> 00:21:48,310
(Cha Seung Yun)

376
00:21:54,350 --> 00:21:55,390
My baby.

377
00:21:56,950 --> 00:21:59,690
Seung Yun, please just stay alive.

378
00:22:12,900 --> 00:22:15,240
Excuse me. It is okay.

379
00:22:16,440 --> 00:22:17,640
You will be okay.

380
00:22:19,610 --> 00:22:20,680
Follow my lead...

381
00:22:21,410 --> 00:22:23,380
and let us take slow, deep breaths.

382
00:22:24,210 --> 00:22:25,220
One.

383
00:22:27,750 --> 00:22:28,750
Two.

384
00:22:33,790 --> 00:22:35,090
You cannot lose consciousness.

385
00:22:35,730 --> 00:22:36,730
One...

386
00:22:37,590 --> 00:22:38,600
Two.

387
00:22:59,250 --> 00:23:00,280
Do Yun!

388
00:23:00,820 --> 00:23:01,820
Do Yun!

389
00:23:02,590 --> 00:23:03,590
Do Yun!

390
00:23:05,860 --> 00:23:10,030
- Did In Sung not tell you?
- Where is my Do Yun?

391
00:23:10,090 --> 00:23:11,090
Where is he?

392
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:14,660
I told your husband,
but I guess you did not hear.

393
00:23:15,100 --> 00:23:17,470
Do Yun kept begging to go too,

394
00:23:17,530 --> 00:23:19,300
so we said
we would take him with us.

395
00:23:19,470 --> 00:23:22,810
- No. Absolutely not.
- Jin Hee.

396
00:23:25,280 --> 00:23:26,880
Do Yun, get out.

397
00:23:27,280 --> 00:23:30,350
- Get out right now.
- Mom, what is wrong?

398
00:23:30,410 --> 00:23:33,380
I want to go with Seung Yun too.

399
00:23:33,850 --> 00:23:37,320
Do Yun, you have somewhere to go
with Mom today.

400
00:23:37,790 --> 00:23:39,620
Come on, be a good boy.
Listen to Mom.

401
00:23:40,990 --> 00:23:41,990
Okay.

402
00:23:43,130 --> 00:23:45,700
Seung Yun.

403
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:49,830
Aunt Jin Hee, please let Do Yun
come with us. Please?

404
00:23:51,070 --> 00:23:54,070
Jin Hee, what is wrong?
You suddenly have somewhere to go?

405
00:23:54,370 --> 00:23:56,110
Were you not just about
to leave for work?

406
00:23:56,840 --> 00:23:58,740
Well, you see...

407
00:23:59,910 --> 00:24:01,650
Do Yun seems to be catching a cold.

408
00:24:01,710 --> 00:24:03,680
It would be terrible
if he passed it to Seung Yun.

409
00:24:04,250 --> 00:24:05,920
I was going to take him
to the doctor first.

410
00:24:06,850 --> 00:24:09,720
- Mom, I do not feel sick at all.
- Listen to me.

411
00:24:11,560 --> 00:24:12,890
You have a fever.

412
00:24:13,890 --> 00:24:17,360
Please go ahead and leave.
Do Yun's forehead is hot right now.

413
00:24:17,790 --> 00:24:20,060
That is a shame, Do Yun.

414
00:24:20,760 --> 00:24:22,900
But you should listen
to your mother.

415
00:24:23,330 --> 00:24:24,840
That is what a good boy does.

416
00:24:24,970 --> 00:24:27,640
If you get sick,
Grandma will be very worried.

417
00:24:29,340 --> 00:24:31,340
Then take him
to the doctor first, Jin Hee.

418
00:24:32,580 --> 00:24:34,580
I feel bad that it is just us going.

419
00:24:35,410 --> 00:24:37,550
It cannot be helped.
Please get going.

420
00:24:38,250 --> 00:24:39,720
Do not worry about the house.

421
00:24:40,880 --> 00:24:41,890
Okay.

422
00:25:10,110 --> 00:25:11,550
The memory of that morning...

423
00:25:12,820 --> 00:25:15,320
was the very first starting point
of all my current suspicions.

424
00:25:16,450 --> 00:25:18,690
I sincerely hope
my suspicions are wrong.

425
00:25:19,890 --> 00:25:21,930
My aunt, Jeon Jin Hee.

426
00:25:31,840 --> 00:25:35,510
If I am even one minute late,
he acts like there is no mercy.

427
00:25:36,440 --> 00:25:38,980
(Onjeong Station)

428
00:25:40,340 --> 00:25:41,580
(No Results Found)

429
00:25:42,180 --> 00:25:43,580
What kind of person
in this day and age...

430
00:25:43,650 --> 00:25:44,810
does not even use social media?

431
00:25:45,620 --> 00:25:47,750
It is not like
I know his phone number.

432
00:25:47,820 --> 00:25:49,120
I cannot even send him
a direct message.

433
00:25:52,260 --> 00:25:54,590
I am only waiting
exactly five minutes.

434
00:26:03,830 --> 00:26:07,000
I can finally breathe.
Why is it so hot today?

435
00:26:07,570 --> 00:26:09,110
I am sorry I am late. Let's go.

436
00:26:12,380 --> 00:26:14,740
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

437
00:26:17,110 --> 00:26:20,380
(Regular Deposit: 200 Dollars
Additional Deposit: 150 Dollars)

438
00:26:23,650 --> 00:26:26,460
To think of the effort it took me
to save this up until this age.

439
00:26:29,360 --> 00:26:32,260
I must be crazy.
What in the world am I thinking?

440
00:26:34,530 --> 00:26:38,670
Mrs. Choi, should we have
a strong cup of coffee?

441
00:26:39,040 --> 00:26:40,940
It is past our coffee time.

442
00:26:41,370 --> 00:26:43,240
Make two cups
and drink them yourself.

443
00:26:43,640 --> 00:26:48,410
Why, Mrs. Choi?
You love sweet instant coffee.

444
00:26:49,550 --> 00:26:52,450
Lately, for some reason,
everything tastes bitter to me.

445
00:26:53,950 --> 00:26:57,820
The reason is obvious.
Your two grandsons...

446
00:26:57,950 --> 00:26:59,260
caused huge trouble
and came back home...

447
00:26:59,320 --> 00:27:00,320
to freeload off you.

448
00:27:01,990 --> 00:27:03,030
By the way,

449
00:27:03,290 --> 00:27:06,300
my sister has been staring
at her bankbook for a while now.

450
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:08,230
I wonder how much is in there.

451
00:27:10,530 --> 00:27:12,740
She still has not come
to her senses.

452
00:27:13,340 --> 00:27:15,940
How can a person be so foolish?

453
00:27:16,940 --> 00:27:18,310
Why does she not realize...

454
00:27:18,380 --> 00:27:20,440
that children are only yours
when they are in your arms?

455
00:27:21,440 --> 00:27:24,050
What is the point of telling her
until I am blue in the face?

456
00:27:24,410 --> 00:27:27,280
If she wants to ruin her own life,
who is going to stop her?

457
00:27:28,790 --> 00:27:32,020
Should I go and see
how much is in there, Mrs. Choi?

458
00:27:32,390 --> 00:27:33,660
There is an old saying.

459
00:27:33,720 --> 00:27:36,060
Holding in your curiosity
shortens your lifespan.

460
00:27:51,610 --> 00:27:53,580
(Regular Payment 200 Dollars,
Total 80,000 Dollars)

461
00:27:53,910 --> 00:27:55,910
I have to pay for
our Da Mi's wedding.

462
00:27:56,710 --> 00:28:00,050
I saved this money
to marry off my daughter.

463
00:28:09,730 --> 00:28:11,730
(Mission: Mompossible)

464
00:28:11,930 --> 00:28:13,960
Are you telling me to go
to Mi Mi's Chicken Soup...

465
00:28:14,030 --> 00:28:15,470
and deliver this right now?

466
00:28:15,830 --> 00:28:16,830
What?

467
00:28:16,900 --> 00:28:19,270
Mi Mi's Chicken Soup.
If I were Su Ah's dad,

468
00:28:19,370 --> 00:28:20,370
I would learn the kitchen work...

469
00:28:20,440 --> 00:28:21,910
from the crack of dawn.

470
00:28:22,340 --> 00:28:23,570
Why are you only looking
at clothes...

471
00:28:24,010 --> 00:28:25,280
when you want to make them?

472
00:28:25,440 --> 00:28:26,440
What else should I look at?

473
00:28:26,640 --> 00:28:27,840
I'm at a clothing store,
so I look at clothes.

474
00:28:29,480 --> 00:28:31,480
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
